  "worked_solution": "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{6}^{x}-4}{{3}^{x}+c} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({6}^{x}-4)}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({3}^{x}+c)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-4}{{3}^{2}+c} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{9+c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $4,$ we can equate the above with $4,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{9+c} & =4 \\\\ 9+c & =8 \\\\ c & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
